# =============================================================================
# PUBLICATION POLICY — settled 2026-08-05. Read before adding or removing lines.
#
# Rule: the repository contains what a USER or CONTRIBUTOR needs. It does not
# contain what the maintainer needs in order to run the project.
#
# PUBLISHED (do not add these to this file):
#   README.md               what it is, how to run it
#   WHITEPAPER.md           architecture, feasibility, limits
#   CRYPTO_FOUNDATIONS.md   what is cryptographically established vs tested
#   SECURITY.md             threat model, fixed vulnerabilities, reporting
#   CONTRIBUTING.md         design principles and contribution rules
#   THESIS.md               category, privacy model, naming history
#   PATH_TO_MASSES.md       free-tier economics, illustrative budget, milestones
#   LICENSE_RIGHTS.md       what MIT does and does not grant
#   GRANT_ONE_PAGER.md      public funding summary
#   AUTHORS.md              provenance
#   LICENSE, blindkeep/, tests/, demo.py, requirements.txt
#
# NOT PUBLISHED (listed below):
#   secrets, personal cockpit and task board, working notes, unfiled drafts.
#
# The distinction is not sensitivity alone. An illustrative budget split is fine
# in a public one-pager; actual line items in an unfiled application are not.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRETS — never commit. data/client/master.key decrypts every record, and
# data/node/identity.pem is a node's signing key. Publishing either destroys
# the guarantees this project is built on.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/node/
data/client/
*.pem
*.key
*.key.sealed
!requirements.txt
data/key_backup.ack

# Node runtime state under ANY data dir, not just the default one. `--data-dir`
# takes an arbitrary path, so a rule naming `data/node/` only covers the node
# nobody renamed: `data/memory_node/` slipped past it with 168 committable
# files. Match the shape a node leaves behind instead of one directory name.
data/*/records/
data/*/head.json
data/pin.json

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Personal cockpit and task board. Local working tools carrying private roadmap
# and task state. Their CLI subcommands register only when these files exist,
# so a clone never advertises a command it cannot run.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
dashboard.py
data/plan.json
blindkeep/progress.py

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Working notes and unfiled drafts.
#   GRANT_PROPOSAL.md      real budget line items and a pre-submission checklist
#                          (the public summary is GRANT_ONE_PAGER.md)
#   HANDOFF_NEXT_TODOS.md  task handoff between maintainers, not project docs
#   COORDINATION.md        shared working surface — READ THIS BEFORE EDITING
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
GRANT_PROPOSAL.md
GRANT_ZCG_ZK.md
HANDOFF_NEXT_TODOS.md
COORDINATION.md

# Local runtime state
data/peers.json
*.log
*.jsonl

circuits/target/
Cargo.lock

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
*.whl
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Environment / editors / OS
.env
.env.*
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
